# HTML Quality Rules

## Structure Requirements
- Must have DOCTYPE declaration
- Must have html, head, and body tags
- Proper nesting of elements

## Head Section
- Must have title tag
- Should have meta charset (UTF-8)
- Should have viewport meta tag
- Should have meta description

## Accessibility
- Images must have alt attributes
- Form inputs must have labels
- Use semantic HTML elements (header, nav, main, etc.)
- Proper heading hierarchy (h1 > h2 > h3)

## Performance
- Minimize inline CSS/JS
- Use external resources efficiently
- Keep file size reasonable

## Code Style
- Maximum line length: 150 characters
- Consistent indentation (2 or 4 spaces)
- Lowercase tags and attributes
- Quote all attributes

## Scoring
- Missing DOCTYPE: -10 points
- Missing title: -10 points
- Missing viewport: -5 points
- Missing alt attributes: -2 points each
- File too long (>1000 lines): -10 points
